# Journal — {{YYYY-MM}}

> **The lookback ledger** (Memory v2). One file per month at `memory/journal/YYYY-MM.md`, created automatically. Append-only — never edit or reorder.
> One line per **event**: `- YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM · <briefing> · <C-/I-/ref or —> · <event> · <text ≤200 chars> · #tag [#tag]`
> Events: `opened · closed · state · decision · fact · calendar · sent · incident · evidence · insight · review`.
> Steady state ("still open", "re-verified", "Day 46") is **not** an event and is never written.
> Write lines with the script (it validates format, date heading and tags):
> `python3 tools/memory_maint.py journal --job evening --ref C-0007 --event closed --text "Coffee happened, great catch-up" --tags "#friends"`
> Read it back: `python3 tools/memory_maint.py lookback --tag "#friends" --month 2026-05` · `--id C-0007` · `--event decision --days 90`

